@section 20.5 | Insects and Silk

@q 35:17-22

**Insects** have 6 legs and 3 body parts. Cockroach **blood is colourless** because it has no haemoglobin; its blood carries food, not oxygen (tracheae carry air directly). Only **female mosquitoes** suck blood (for egg development) and they are slightly larger, with bigger wings; males feed on plant juices.

@table
Product | Insect / source
**Silk** | Silkworm *Bombyx mori* (mulberry); **tasar**, **muga** (Assam), **eri** ("Ahimsa"/peace silk) from other moths
**Gossamer** silk | **Spiders**
**Honey**, beeswax | *Apis* honey bees
**Lac** | Lac insect *Laccifer (Kerria) lacca*
**Pearl** | **Oyster** (a mollusc), not an insect
**Helicoverpa armigera** | **Cotton bollworm**, a major **pest**
@end

@section 20.6 | Animals of Special Habitats

@q 35:23-24

@q 35:25

Snake **fangs** are modified **maxillary** (upper jaw) teeth connected to venom glands, which are modified **salivary** glands. **Xerocoles** live in deserts; arboreal animals in trees; fossorial animals burrow.

@section 20.7 | Special Plants

@q 35:26-30

@table
Plant type | Examples
**Insectivorous** (catch insects for **nitrogen**) | **Nepenthes** (pitcher plant; *N. khasiana* of **Meghalaya**), Drosera (sundew), Utricularia (bladderwort), Venus flytrap
**Stem parasite** | **Cuscuta** (dodder, amarbel)
**Root parasite** | **Sandalwood** (partial), Orobanche, Striga
**Epiphyte** | **Orchids**, Spanish moss
Hydrophyte | Lotus (*Nelumbo*), water hyacinth, Hydrilla
Saprophyte | Monotropa (Indian pipe), most fungi
@end

Insectivorous plants are **green** and make their own food; they grow in bogs poor in nitrogen and get it by digesting insects. *Nyctanthes* is harsingar, *Nelumbo* the lotus and *Nicotiana* tobacco.

@q 35:38

@q 35:46

**Mycorrhiza** is a fungus-root partnership that helps plants absorb phosphorus and water. **Leghaemoglobin**, a red pigment, protects the nitrogen-fixing enzyme in the **root nodules of legumes** from oxygen.

