@q 35:39-40

@q 35:41-43

**Garlic** smells of **sulphur** compounds (allicin). **Onions** release *syn*-propanethial-S-oxide formed from **sulfenic acid**, which irritates the eyes. **Capsaicin** makes chillies hot (Bhut Jolokia of the north-east is among the hottest).

@q 35:44-45

@q 35:47

**Triticale** (wheat × rye, *Triticum* × *Secale*) is the first **man-made cereal**. Pomato is a potato-tomato graft, not a cereal. **Fibres from stems** (bast fibres): jute, hemp, sunn hemp, flax; **cotton** is a seed hair.

@section 20.9 | Ecological Terms and Pigments

@q 35:48

@q 35:49-51

Desert plants (xerophytes) have **long roots** to reach deep water, **succulent** stems or leaves to store water (cactus, aloe), and small or spiny leaves to cut water loss; the high soil temperature is not the reason. Most water is taken up by **root hairs**.

@q 35:52-55

**Herbivores** are **primary** consumers; carnivores that eat them are secondary consumers. Producers are autotrophs, decomposers saprotrophs.

@q 35:56-57

@table
Pigment | Colour in
**Anthocyanin** | **Red apple**, red cabbage, purple brinjal, jamun (water-soluble)
**Lycopene** | **Tomato**, watermelon
**Carotene** | Carrot, mango (orange; vitamin A precursor)
**Caricaxanthin** | **Papaya** (yellow)
Xanthophyll | Yellow leaves
Capsanthin | Red chillies
@end

@q 35:58-60

@trap
**Gerontology = ageing**, osteology = bones, **viticulture = grapes**, pisciculture = fish. Early atmosphere had **no oxygen**. **Mutation theory = de Vries.** Bacteria have **no chloroplasts**. **Seahorse is a fish**, bat and whale are mammals, **spider is not an insect**, **octopus is a mollusc**. Frogs have a **3-chambered** heart. **Pearl** is not from an insect. **Nepenthes** is insectivorous, not parasitic. **Potato = stem**, **sweet potato = root**. **Clove = flower bud**, **saffron = stigma**. Red apple = **anthocyanin**, tomato = **lycopene**.
@end

